<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Work with pipelines" id="Azure-DevOps-Pipelines">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Open: <ui-path>View | Tool Windows | AZD Pipelines</ui-path></p>
        <p>Run a pipeline: <shortcut>Alt+Insert</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ N</shortcut>) in the tool window</p>
        <p>Configure: <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Pipeline Settings</ui-path></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Find, run, inspect, cancel and rerun Azure Pipelines runs, read stage logs and view the stage diagram.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Run Azure Pipelines, watch runs, read logs and view the stage diagram in the IDE.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Run and monitor Azure Pipelines in JetBrains IDEs with the AZD plugin: filter runs, pass parameters,
        read stage logs, rerun failed jobs and view stage diagrams.</web-summary>

    <p>
        The <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window lists the pipeline runs of the current repository and opens each run in its own tab.
        For the YAML schema, approvals and Node.js options, see
        <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="pipeline-settings">Pipeline Settings</a>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Find a pipeline run" id="view-pipelines">
        <p>
            The tool window is available in projects with an Azure DevOps Git remote.
            If you are not signed in, it shows the sign-in options; see
            <a href="Azd-Installation.topic" anchor="connect">Connect to Azure DevOps</a>.
            The first tab, named after the repository, lists the runs of every pipeline in that repository, newest first.
            Each row shows the run name, commit message, branch, result and the person who requested the run.
        </p>
        <img src="azd_pipelines_list.png" alt="AZD Pipelines tool window listing runs with the quick filter, filter chips and run results" width="422" border-effect="rounded"/>

        <procedure title="Find and open a run" id="open-run">
            <step>
                <p>Type in the search field, or click the filter icon and select a quick filter:
                    <control>All</control>, <control>In Progress</control>, <control>Triggered by me</control> or <control>Current branch</control>.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Narrow the list with the filter chips: <control>Status</control>, <control>Result</control>, <control>Reason</control>,
                    <control>Triggered by</control>, <control>Branch</control> and <control>Pipeline Name</control>.
                    <control>Pipeline Name</control> accepts several pipelines.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>To change the order, click the sort icon and select <control>Default (newest first)</control>, <control>Started</control>,
                    <control>Finished</control>, <control>Build Number</control> or <control>Pipeline Name</control>.
                    Select <control>Descending</control> to reverse it.</p>
                <img src="sort_pipeline_and_pr_inline_button.png" alt="Sort popup of the AZD Pipelines run list with Default (newest first) selected"
                     width="510" border-effect="rounded"/>
                <img src="azd_pipelines_sort.png" alt="Sort popup open over the AZD Pipelines run list" width="422" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Double-click a run, or right-click it and select <control>Show Pipeline Details</control>, to open it in a new tab.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>

        <p>The context menu of a run also has these actions:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Open Pipeline in Browser">Opens the run on Azure DevOps.</def>
            <def title="Copy Pipeline URL">Copies the web URL of the run.</def>
            <def title="Filter by This Pipeline">Shows only the runs of the same pipeline.</def>
            <def title="Refresh Builds List">Reloads the list.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            To refresh the list on a schedule, select <control>Auto-refresh pipelines</control> in
            <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="general-configuration">Preferences</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Run a pipeline" id="trigger-pipelines">
        <procedure title="Queue a pipeline run" id="trigger-pipeline">
            <step>
                <p>In the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> title bar, click <control>Run Pipeline</control> (the <control>+</control> icon),
                    or press <shortcut>Alt+Insert</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ N</shortcut>) while the tool window has focus.</p>
                <p>The <control>Run Pipeline</control> tab opens.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In <control>Pipeline</control>, start typing the pipeline name and select it.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In <control>Branch</control>, select the branch to build.
                    If the branch does not exist, the pipeline uses its default branch.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Under <control>Pipeline parameters</control>, set the runtime parameters the pipeline defines.</p>
                <img src="azd_pipelines_run_form.png" alt="Run Pipeline tab with a pipeline, a branch and runtime parameters filled in" width="422" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Optional: if the pipeline has variables that can be set at queue time, click the browse button in <control>Variables</control>
                    under <control>Advanced options</control> to edit them in the <control>Pipeline Variables</control> dialog.</p>
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_variables_dialog.png" alt="Pipeline Variables dialog with two queue-time variables" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Click <control>Run Pipeline</control>.</p>
                <p>AZD queues the run and opens it in a new tab.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>To queue an open run again, see <a anchor="run-details"/>.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Inspect a run" id="run-details">
        <p>A run tab shows:</p>
        <list>
            <li>The run number and a status label, such as <control>SUCCESS</control>, <control>FAILED</control> or <control>IN PROGRESS</control>.</li>
            <li><control>Repository and version</control>: links to the repository, the commit and, for runs started by a pull request or by its merge, the pull request.
                A pull request of this repository opens in the <control>AZD Pull Requests</control> tool window if
                <a href="Azd-Settings-Configuration.topic" anchor="general-configuration">Open AZD links in tool window</a> is selected;
                the other links open in the browser.</li>
            <li><control>Time started and elapsed</control>, and how long the run waited for an agent.</li>
            <li>The stage, job and task tree with live durations.
                A run that was rerun shows an <control>Attempt #n</control> node for each attempt, and the latest one is marked <control>(latest)</control>.</li>
        </list>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_run_details.png" alt="Run tab with the status label, repository and version, timing and an expanded stage tree with two attempts" -->

        <p>Right-click a stage, job or task in the tree for these actions:</p>
        <img src="pipelines_details_actions.png" alt="Context menu of a task in the run tree with Show Logs, Run Pipeline and Jump to YAML"
             width="489" border-effect="rounded"/>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_stage_menu.png" alt="Context menu of a task in the run tree with Show Logs, Run Pipeline, Jump to YAML and the stage URL actions" replaces="pipelines_details_actions.png" -->
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Show Logs">Opens the log of the task in the editor. See <a anchor="stage-logs"/>.</def>
            <def title="Run Pipeline">Opens the <control>Run Pipeline</control> tab with the pipeline and branch of this run filled in.</def>
            <def title="Jump to YAML">Opens the pipeline definition file.</def>
            <def title="Open Stage in Browser">Opens the selected stage, job or task on Azure DevOps.</def>
            <def title="Copy Stage URL">Copies its web URL.</def>
            <def title="Refresh Details">Reloads the run.</def>
        </deflist>

        <procedure title="Cancel a run or rerun failed jobs" id="cancel-rerun" type="choices">
            <p>The button at the bottom of the run tab changes with the state of the run.</p>
            <step>
                <p>To stop a running pipeline, click <control>Cancel</control>.
                    The button shows <control>Cancelling…</control> until Azure DevOps stops the run.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>To rerun the failed jobs of a finished run, click <control>Rerun failed jobs</control>, then click <control>Yes</control> to confirm.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="View stage logs" id="stage-logs">
        <p>
            Double-click a task in the run tree, or right-click it and select <control>Show Logs</control>.
            The log opens in an editor tab named <control>&lt;task&gt; logs</control> and loads one page at a time.
        </p>
        <img src="stage_logs_in_editor_with_pagination_and_ai_invocation.png"
             alt="Run tree next to a task log in the editor with the paging and AI toolbar"
             width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_stage_log.png" alt="Stage log in the editor with the Earlier Lines, Later Lines, Jump to End and Chat with AI About This Log toolbar" replaces="stage_logs_in_editor_with_pagination_and_ai_invocation.png" -->
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Earlier Lines">Shows the previous page of the log.</def>
            <def title="Later Lines">Shows the next page.</def>
            <def title="Jump to End">Shows the end of the log.</def>
            <def title="Chat with AI About This Log">Sends the log to an AI provider. See <a anchor="log-analysis"/>.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            The status line shows which lines are on screen, for example <control>Showing lines 1–3000 of 8200</control>.
            A page holds 3000 lines by default; change it with the <code>azd.pipeline.log.page.lines</code> registry key.
            Sections that the pipeline marks with <code>##[group]</code> are folded under their group name; click the fold to expand one.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Analyze a log with AI" id="log-analysis">
        <p>Ask an AI provider to explain a failure and suggest a fix, then ask follow-up questions about the same log.</p>
        <procedure title="Analyze a stage log with AI" id="analyze-logs-with-ai">
            <step>
                <p>Open the log of a task, as described in <a anchor="stage-logs"/>.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the log toolbar, click <control>Chat with AI About This Log</control> and select a provider.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Read the analysis in the new <control>AI Log</control> tab of the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window.</p>
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_ai_log_chat.png" alt="AI Log tab in the AZD Pipelines tool window with an analysis of a failed build log" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Optional: type a question in <control>Ask a follow-up about this log</control> and click <control>Send</control>.
                    Click <control>Stop</control> to cancel an answer.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            The list shows the providers enabled in <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | AI Settings</ui-path>.
            To add a provider or switch it off, see <a href="Azd-AI.topic" anchor="ai-providers">AI providers</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="View the stage diagram" id="pipeline-diagram">
        <p>
            In a run tab, click <control>View Pipeline Diagram</control>.
            The <control>Pipeline !&lt;id&gt;</control> editor tab opens on the <control>Stages</control> tab with a graph of the stages and their dependencies.
            The graph updates while the run is in progress.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pipelines_diagram.png" alt="Pipeline stage diagram in the editor with one failed stage and the diagram toolbar" -->
        <list>
            <li>Click a stage to show or hide its jobs.</li>
            <li>Drag a stage to move it.</li>
            <li>Use the toolbar to <control>Change Layout</control>, <control>Zoom In</control>, <control>Fit to Screen</control>,
                <control>Zoom Out</control>, <control>Open Pipeline in Browser</control>, <control>Copy Pipeline URL</control>
                or <control>Refresh Details</control>.</li>
            <li>The <control>Tests</control> tab shows the test results of the run; see <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Tests.topic"/>.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            To rerun the failed jobs of a run, click <control>Rerun failed jobs</control> at the bottom of the run tab; see <a anchor="cancel-rerun"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Approvals, tests, metrics and YAML" id="more-pipeline-tasks">
        <p id="approvals">
            To approve, reject or defer a run that waits for you, see <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Approvals.topic"/>.
        </p>
        <p id="tests">
            To review test results and associate tests with test cases, see <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Tests.topic"/>.
        </p>
        <p id="pipeline-metrics">
            To see pass rates, durations, queue times and agent pools, see <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Metrics.topic"/>.
        </p>
        <p id="yaml-injection">
            For completion and validation in <path>azure-pipelines.yml</path> and other pipeline files, see <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Yaml.topic"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Keyboard shortcuts" id="pipeline-shortcuts">
        <p>These shortcuts work while the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window has focus.</p>
        <table style="header-row">
            <tr>
                <td>Action</td>
                <td>Windows and Linux</td>
                <td>macOS</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><control>Open AZD Pipelines Settings</control></td>
                <td><shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut></td>
                <td><shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><control>Run Pipeline</control></td>
                <td><shortcut>Alt+Insert</shortcut></td>
                <td><shortcut>⌘ N</shortcut></td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        <p>
            <control>Refresh Builds List</control> and <control>Refresh Details</control> use the IDE <control>Refresh</control> shortcut.
            To see or change it, open <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

